---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import SideNav from '../components/SideNav.astro';
import {
  BRAND,
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  GITHUB_REPO_URL,
  LICENCE_PROVIDER,
  LICENCE_PROVIDER_URL,
  OWNER,
  REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS,
  TERMS_EFFECTIVE_DATE,
} from '../config';

const sections = [
  { id: 'code', label: 'The code: MIT' },
  { id: 'pro', label: 'Pro licences' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refunds' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'Warranty and liability' },
  { id: 'trademarks', label: 'Names and trademarks' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms and licence"
  description="The code is MIT. Pro is a one-time licence key. Refunds within 14 days. That is most of it; the rest is below."
  path="/terms"
  kicker={`${BRAND} / Terms`}
  effective={TERMS_EFFECTIVE_DATE}
  current="terms"
>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <SideNav title="Sections" items={sections.map((s) => ({ href: `#${s.id}`, label: s.label }))} />
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="code">The code: MIT</h2>
  <p>
    All {BRAND} extensions (Arbor, Reroute, CookieSweep) and this website are released under the
    <a href="https://opensource.org/license/mit" rel="noopener">MIT licence</a>. The full text is in the
    <code>LICENSE</code> file of <a href={GITHUB_REPO_URL} rel="noopener">the repository</a>. In short: you may
    use, copy, modify, build and redistribute the code, including for commercial purposes, provided the copyright
    and licence notice are kept. The software is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;, without warranty.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in the Pro terms below restricts what the MIT licence grants you over the code. A Pro licence is not a
    software licence in the copyright sense; it is a key that unlocks Pro features in the official builds, and a way
    to pay for their continued maintenance.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pro">Pro licences</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What you buy.</strong> A licence key for one {BRAND} extension (Arbor Pro or Reroute Pro), sold as a
      one-time purchase. There is no subscription and no renewal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Who may use it.</strong> The key is personal to the purchaser and may be activated on all browser
      profiles and devices that the purchaser uses. Team or organisation use requires one key per person.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What it unlocks.</strong> The Pro features listed on the product page at the time of purchase, in the
      official builds distributed through the Chrome Web Store and Microsoft Edge Add-ons, for all future versions of
      that extension. For Arbor Pro today that means scheduled local backups (kept on your own computer) and a
      licence valid across all your browser profiles; features marked &ldquo;planned&rdquo; on a product page are
      not part of the purchase until they ship. If a Pro feature is later moved to the free tier, that is a gift,
      not a breach.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Activation.</strong> Keys are issued and validated by {LICENCE_PROVIDER}, our merchant of record.
      Activation sends the key and a random instance identifier to {LICENCE_PROVIDER}; see the product&rsquo;s
      privacy policy. If {LICENCE_PROVIDER} is unreachable, already-activated features keep working.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Restrictions.</strong> Do not share, resell or publish a key. Keys found in public places or used far
      beyond a single person&rsquo;s plausible use may be deactivated after we try to contact you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>If the project ends.</strong> Should {BRAND} stop maintaining an extension, we will publish a final
      release in which Pro features are unlocked for everyone. The MIT-licensed source remains available regardless.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    If a Pro licence does not work for you for any reason, request a refund within {REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS} days of
    purchase. Refunds are processed by {LICENCE_PROVIDER}: reply to your purchase receipt email, or write to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with your order number. Refunded keys are deactivated.
    Statutory rights in your country that go beyond this are not affected.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranty">Warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The extensions are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;. To the extent permitted by law, {OWNER} disclaims all warranties,
    express or implied, and is not liable for any loss of data, sessions, tabs, cookies or profits arising from
    their use. Arbor in particular manages the tabs you ask it to manage; keep backups of anything you cannot afford
    to lose, and check the recovery screen before dismissing it. Where a jurisdiction does not allow this exclusion,
    liability is limited to the amount you paid for the Pro licence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trademarks">Names and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    {BRAND}, Arbor, Reroute and CookieSweep are names used by {OWNER} for this project. Chrome is a trademark of
    Google LLC; Edge is a trademark of Microsoft Corporation; {LICENCE_PROVIDER} is a trademark of its owner. Tabs Outliner, Redirector, Cookie AutoDelete and ClearURLs are separate projects by their own authors;
    their names appear on this site only to state, factually, which file formats our extensions can import or which
    publicly licensed rule catalog is bundled. {BRAND} is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by any of
    them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may change. The version in effect at the time of your purchase governs that purchase. Changes are
    published here with a new effective date and recorded in the website repository&rsquo;s history.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {OWNER}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
    Payments and receipts: <a href={LICENCE_PROVIDER_URL} rel="noopener">{LICENCE_PROVIDER}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
